# A coaxial line: a cylinder seen from the side, the leads meeting its two ends.
kind transmissionline
convention A coaxial transmission line: a cylinder, one end seen whole and the other as its near half.
pin 1 -100 0
pin 2 100 0
line -100 0 -60 0
line 60 0 100 0
ellipse -50 0 10 25
ellipse 50 0 10 25 -90 180
line -50 -25 50 -25
line -50 25 50 25
